{"ocrText": "straction and tried to be literal-minded about\nit. They spent\ntheir lives doing quite the opposite.\nRita thought that that sort of imaginative ability could help a\nperson. A pleasant notion, to think of dirty clothes piled high\nin the laundry basket as Monet's haystack. To see the melting\nice cream as a cloud.\nDear Lucy\u2014How you two loved bubbles! Td try to do the\ndishes and you two would reach around me and dip your\nblowers into the sink and lift them out and blow and blow.\nI\nhad to put so much detergent in the water that the dishes al-\nmost slipped out ofmy hands.\nIt took forever to rinse them. To\nthink that I ever thought of all that fun as frustrating. There\nwe'd be, bubbles\nall around us,\na storm of them mirroring\neverything in the kitchen\u2014all those mundane things, stepstools\nand canisters, become for a second mere flashes of color that\npopped and collided.\nThey were endlessly fascinated with lightning bugs. They\nwould beg to sleep with a jar of them in their room, air holes\npunched with the ice pick in the metal top. They'd put\nit by\nthe night-light because they thought they blinked more when\nthere was some source of light.\nIt had\nits equivalent in Chris-\ntian thinking\u2014all the little children prospering under God's ra-\ndiance.\nRita felt sure that their religious training had been neglected.\nThey had memorized the recipe for chocolate chip cookies be-\nfore they knew the Ten Commandments. They were so wor-\nshipful of each other that\nit was hard to make Mary take on any\nreal character. The apostles paled by comparison with the lives\nof their\nstuffed\nanimals.\nShe should have\nsent\nthe\ngirls\nto\nchurch\nregularly.\nEventually,\nthe\nminister might have\npre-\nvailed.\nHe would not have prevailed.\nIt got to the point where no\nman could persuade them of anything. Jane didn't even take\nmen seriously enough to bother finding one who was\nbetter\nthan the rest. Except that there was a similarity in the men she\nchose. She liked childish men. Not because she felt threatened\nby men or because she wanted to have power over them, but\nbecause\nit became increasingly difficult as she got older to find\n21", "textLayer": [{"text": "straction", "x": 6.21, "y": 5.17, "w": 10.57, "h": 1.48, "fontSize": 7.4}, {"text": "and", "x": 18.29, "y": 4.93, "w": 4.27, "h": 1.8, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "tried", "x": 23.98, "y": 5.17, "w": 5.69, "h": 1.44, "fontSize": 7.2}, {"text": "to", "x": 31.09, "y": 5.17, "w": 2.27, "h": 1.44, "fontSize": 7.2}, {"text": "be", "x": 34.74, "y": 4.92, "w": 2.75, "h": 1.74, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "literal-minded", "x": 38.91, "y": 5.01, "w": 17.44, "h": 1.58, "fontSize": 7.9}, {"text": "about", "x": 57.82, "y": 4.91, "w": 6.78, "h": 1.71, "fontSize": 8.6}, {"text": "it.", "x": 66.11, "y": 5.5, "w": 2.18, "h": 0.92, "fontSize": 4.6}, {"text": "They", "x": 69.81, "y": 4.6, "w": 6.63, "h": 2.1, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "spent", "x": 78.01, "y": 4.98, "w": 6.4, "h": 1.62, "fontSize": 8.1}, {"text": "their", "x": 6.16, "y": 7.37, "w": 5.78, "h": 1.46, "fontSize": 7.3}, {"text": "lives", "x": 13.13, "y": 7.44, "w": 5.26, "h": 1.33, "fontSize": 6.6}, {"text": "doing", "x": 19.57, "y": 7.13, "w": 6.92, "h": 1.75, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "quite", "x": 27.58, "y": 7.24, "w": 6.16, "h": 1.56, "fontSize": 7.8}, {"text": "the", "x": 34.88, "y": 7.23, "w": 3.74, "h": 1.58, "fontSize": 7.9}, {"text": "opposite.", "x": 39.72, "y": 7.22, "w": 10.99, "h": 1.54, "fontSize": 7.7}, {"text": "Rita", "x": 9.24, "y": 9.49, "w": 4.93, "h": 1.56, "fontSize": 7.8}, {"text": "thought", "x": 15.07, "y": 9.35, "w": 9.62, "h": 1.74, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "that", "x": 25.64, "y": 9.52, "w": 4.69, "h": 1.48, "fontSize": 7.4}, {"text": "that", "x": 31.28, "y": 9.53, "w": 4.64, "h": 1.47, "fontSize": 7.3}, {"text": "sort", "x": 36.92, "y": 9.53, "w": 4.5, "h": 1.42, "fontSize": 7.1}, {"text": "of", "x": 42.37, "y": 9.43, "w": 2.46, "h": 1.56, "fontSize": 7.8}, 